# These wheels ARE tracked, unlike the usual convention.
#
# `backend/server/pyproject.toml` sources `agentkit`, `deerflow-harness` and
# `deerflow-extension-api` from the .whl files in this directory rather than from the
# monorepo source tree. That is what makes `uv sync` work on a machine that has only
# this project directory: the three in-repo packages resolve like any other
# dependency, with no `libs/agentkit` checkout and no assumed directory depth.
#
# Ignoring them (`*`, as this file used to say) breaks that completely — the lock
# pins `wheels/agentkit-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl`, so a checkout without it fails to
# install. Total size is ~2.8MB, dominated by the 2.8MB harness wheel.
#
# Regenerate with `./scripts/build-release.sh --update` after ANY change to the
# vendored DeerFlow source or agentkit — a stale wheel silently installs old code,
# which is worse than a failed install.
*
!*.whl
!README.md
!.gitignore
# Which upstream revision the wheels were built from. Data, not source: it is what
# lets a rebuild fetch exactly the right commit on demand instead of requiring a
# checkout of the 203 MB upstream in every clone.
!DEERFLOW_SOURCE.txt
